{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prose-intro-q-resolvent-wick","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Prose","doco:Section"],"label":"prose:intro-q-resolvent-wick","kind":"prose","text":"intro-q-resolvent-wick.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prose:intro-q-resolvent-wick\"></a><p>Define the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-resolvent <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R_q(s) = (s + \\widehat{\\Delta_q})^{-1}</code> as a categorical Laplace transform of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-heat semigroup. The categorical Wick rotation collapses the Laplace and Fourier transforms into a single grouplike pairing against <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\exp_q \\in G(\\mathcal{H}_q)</code> evaluated at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">s</code> or <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">i\\xi</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/intro-q-resolvent-wick.md","heading":"","page":"b/prose-intro-q-resolvent-wick","qa":{"counts":{"pass":14,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":5,"unknown":0,"stale":18},"milnor":{"total":1,"notPassing":1}}}
